Audience: compiler and tooling engineers who maintain this spec.

## Scenarios

### Draw IR patch generation

#### patches an image URI change and damages its existing bounds

- Verify: patches an image URI change and damages its existing bounds
   - Expected: patch.damage_rects.len() equals `2)  # oracle: 2 — named expected value from the requirement`
   - Expected: patch.damage_rects[0].x equals `10)  # oracle: 10 — named expected value from the requirement`
   - Expected: patch.damage_rects[0].width equals `30)  # oracle: 30 — named expected value from the requirement`
   - Expected: applied.ok is true
   - Expected: draw_ir_patch_commands_equal(applied.composition, current) is true


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 24 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: patches an image URI change and damages its existing bounds")
# @req: REQ-LIB-COMMON-001
val baseline = draw_ir_composition("rev-1", "scene", DRAW_IR_BACKEND_CPU, [
    draw_ir_batch("batch", DRAW_IR_BACKEND_CPU, _embedding(), [
        draw_ir_image_command("content", 10, 20, 30, 40,
            "wm-content://window/old", [])
    ])
])
val current = draw_ir_composition("rev-2", "scene", DRAW_IR_BACKEND_CPU, [
    draw_ir_batch("batch", DRAW_IR_BACKEND_CPU, _embedding(), [
        draw_ir_image_command("content", 10, 20, 30, 40,
            "wm-content://window/new", [])
    ])
])
val patch = draw_ir_patch_between(baseline, "rev-1", current, "rev-2")
expect(_op_kind_present(
    patch.operations, DRAW_IR_PATCH_OP_UPDATE_STYLE, "content"
)).to_equal(true)
expect(patch.damage_rects.len()).to_equal(2)  # oracle: 2 — named expected value from the requirement
expect(patch.damage_rects[0].x).to_equal(10)  # oracle: 10 — named expected value from the requirement
expect(patch.damage_rects[0].width).to_equal(30)  # oracle: 30 — named expected value from the requirement
val applied = draw_ir_patch_apply(baseline, patch)
expect(applied.ok).to_equal(true)
expect(draw_ir_patch_commands_equal(applied.composition, current)).to_equal(true)
```

</details>

