#### uses edge payload points even when the mirrored command points are stale

- Verify: uses edge payload points even when the mirrored command points are stale
   - Expected: patch.damage_rects.len() equals `2)  # oracle: 2 — named expected value from the requirement`
   - Expected: patch.damage_rects[1].x equals `99)  # oracle: 99 — named expected value from the requirement`
   - Expected: patch.damage_rects[1].y equals `109)  # oracle: 109 — named expected value from the requirement`
   - Expected: patch.damage_rects[1].width equals `23)  # oracle: 23 — named expected value from the requirement`
   - Expected: patch.damage_rects[1].height equals `23)  # oracle: 23 — named expected value from the requirement`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 24 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
step("Verify: uses edge payload points even when the mirrored command points are stale")
val old_edge = draw_ir_edge_command(draw_edge(
    "edge", "a", "b", "straight",
    [draw_ir_point(10, 10), draw_ir_point(20, 20)], []))
var new_edge = old_edge
new_edge.edge = Some(draw_edge(
    "edge", "a", "b", "straight",
    [draw_ir_point(100, 110), draw_ir_point(120, 130)], []))
# Leave new_edge.points at the old values to model an independently
# decoded/stale mirror; retained damage must still cover the payload
# the edge rasterizer actually consumes.
val baseline = draw_ir_composition("rev-1", "scene", DRAW_IR_BACKEND_CPU, [
    draw_ir_batch("batch", DRAW_IR_BACKEND_CPU, _embedding(), [old_edge])
])
val current = draw_ir_composition("rev-2", "scene", DRAW_IR_BACKEND_CPU, [
    draw_ir_batch("batch", DRAW_IR_BACKEND_CPU, _embedding(), [new_edge])
])
val patch = draw_ir_patch_between(baseline, "rev-1", current, "rev-2")
expect(patch.damage_rects.len()).to_equal(2)  # oracle: 2 — named expected value from the requirement
expect(patch.damage_rects[1].x).to_equal(99)  # oracle: 99 — named expected value from the requirement
expect(patch.damage_rects[1].y).to_equal(109)  # oracle: 109 — named expected value from the requirement
expect(patch.damage_rects[1].width).to_equal(23)  # oracle: 23 — named expected value from the requirement
expect(patch.damage_rects[1].height).to_equal(23)  # oracle: 23 — named expected value from the requirement
```

</details>

#### uses stroke payloads despite stale nonzero geometry and ordered styles

- Verify: uses stroke payloads despite stale nonzero geometry and ordered styles
   - Expected: patch.damage_rects[1].x equals `99)  # oracle: 99 — named expected value from the requirement`
   - Expected: patch.damage_rects[1].y equals `99)  # oracle: 99 — named expected value from the requirement`
   - Expected: draw_ir_patch_commands_equal(applied.composition, current) is true


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 33 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
step("Verify: uses stroke payloads despite stale nonzero geometry and ordered styles")
val old_path = draw_ir_path_command("path", [draw_ir_point(10, 10),
    draw_ir_point(20, 20)], [draw_ir_style_prop("stroke-color", "1")])
var new_path = old_path
new_path.points = [draw_ir_point(100, 100), draw_ir_point(120, 120)]
new_path.x = 1
new_path.y = 2
new_path.width = 3
new_path.height = 4
new_path.computed_style = [
    draw_ir_style_prop("stroke-color", "1"),
    draw_ir_style_prop("stroke-color", "2")
]
var old_with_duplicate = old_path
old_with_duplicate.computed_style = [
    draw_ir_style_prop("stroke-color", "1"),
    draw_ir_style_prop("stroke-color", "1")
]
val baseline = draw_ir_composition("rev-1", "scene", DRAW_IR_BACKEND_CPU, [
    draw_ir_batch("batch", DRAW_IR_BACKEND_CPU, _embedding(), [old_with_duplicate])
])
val current = draw_ir_composition("rev-2", "scene", DRAW_IR_BACKEND_CPU, [
    draw_ir_batch("batch", DRAW_IR_BACKEND_CPU, _embedding(), [new_path])
])
val patch = draw_ir_patch_between(baseline, "rev-1", current, "rev-2")
expect(_op_kind_present(
    patch.operations, DRAW_IR_PATCH_OP_UPDATE_GEOMETRY, "path"
)).to_equal(true)
expect(patch.damage_rects[1].x).to_equal(99)  # oracle: 99 — named expected value from the requirement
expect(patch.damage_rects[1].y).to_equal(99)  # oracle: 99 — named expected value from the requirement
val applied = draw_ir_patch_apply(baseline, patch)
expect(draw_ir_patch_commands_equal(applied.composition, current)).to_equal(true)
```

</details>

#### emits an Insert op for a new component with new_bounds set and no old_bounds

- Verify: emits an Insert op for a new component with new_bounds set and no old_bounds
   - Expected: _op_kind_present(patch.operations, DRAW_IR_PATCH_OP_INSERT, "fresh") is true
   - Expected: op.old_bounds.present is false
   - Expected: op.new_bounds.present is true
   - Expected: op.new_bounds.x equals `1)  # oracle: 1 — named expected value from the requirement`
   - Expected: op.new_bounds.y equals `2)  # oracle: 2 — named expected value from the requirement`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 21 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
step("Verify: emits an Insert op for a new component with new_bounds set and no old_bounds")
val baseline = draw_ir_composition("rev-1", "scene", DRAW_IR_BACKEND_CPU, [
    draw_ir_batch("batch", DRAW_IR_BACKEND_CPU, _embedding(), [
        draw_ir_rect("box", 10, 10, 50, 20, 1u32)
    ])
])
val current = draw_ir_composition("rev-2", "scene", DRAW_IR_BACKEND_CPU, [
    draw_ir_batch("batch", DRAW_IR_BACKEND_CPU, _embedding(), [
        draw_ir_rect("box", 10, 10, 50, 20, 1u32),
        draw_ir_rect("fresh", 1, 2, 5, 6, 9u32)
    ])
])
val patch = draw_ir_patch_between(baseline, "rev-1", current, "rev-2")
expect(_op_kind_present(patch.operations, DRAW_IR_PATCH_OP_INSERT, "fresh")).to_equal(true)
for op in patch.operations:
    if op.component_id == "fresh":
        expect(op.old_bounds.present).to_equal(false)
        expect(op.new_bounds.present).to_equal(true)
        expect(op.new_bounds.x).to_equal(1)  # oracle: 1 — named expected value from the requirement
        expect(op.new_bounds.y).to_equal(2)  # oracle: 2 — named expected value from the requirement
```

</details>

